1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,920
This is InventDB Legal.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:10,920
Practice management for law firms, built on InventDB SOAR.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,920
A missed deadline can become a malpractice claim.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,920
A trust account error can become a State Bar complaint.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:22,420
Unbilled time is a fee the firm never collects.

6
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:25,920
InventDB Legal is built around all three.

7
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,920
Sign in with the firm's InventDB account.

8
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:36,920
The firm's day on one page: 730 open matters, 172 deadlines and 176 hearings in the next 30 days.

9
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:42,920
$300,640 of unbilled work, $778,109 owed, and $1.27 million held in trust.

10
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:48,420
Deadlines first. Missed deadlines are a common cause of malpractice claims.

11
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:51,920
The dashboard shows what falls due, soonest first.

12
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:57,920
Each is counted from its rule: here, Rule 8.121(a), ten days from the notice of appeal.

13
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:02,420
Every deadline has an owner, a priority and a count of the days remaining.

14
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:07,420
Every matter carries its statute of limitations date.

15
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:13,420
Hearings, depositions and mediations share one court calendar.

16
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:16,920
Open a busy day to see every appearance.

17
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,420
The docket report lists all 172 deadlines due in the next 30 days.

18
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:26,920
And a workflow emails each attorney their critical deadlines every weekday morning.

19
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:31,920
Then client money: trust account errors are a common cause of State Bar discipline.

20
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:36,920
Each matter shows its trust balance against its retainer and replenish threshold.

21
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:42,920
Every deposit, earned-fee transfer and disbursement is entered on the client's own ledger,

22
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:47,920
with a running balance for every matter, line by line.

23
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:54,920
The monthly reconciliation shows bank clearance, and that no client ledger ever went below zero.

24
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:02,920
Settlements show the gross, the fee, costs, each lien negotiated down, and the net to the client.

25
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:08,920
When a trust balance runs low, a workflow asks a partner before requesting a top-up.

26
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:12,920
Billing: hours never recorded are fees never collected.

27
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:16,920
Time is entered against the matter, as the work is done.

28
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:23,920
Each entry carries UTBMS phase, task and activity codes, the coding insurers and corporate clients ask for.

29
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:29,920
Unbilled work is valued at standard rates: $300,640 across the firm.

30
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:36,920
Invoices show fees, write-downs, costs, payments applied from trust and the balance due.

31
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:43,920
Receivables are aged by client, so the $216,788 over 120 days gets chased first.

32
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:48,920
Change any report by describing the change. Each edit saves a new version.

33
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:52,920
Partners can ask the practice a question in plain English.

34
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:56,920
Analyze plans the queries and answers with a chart.

35
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:01,920
Business Litigation holds the most unbilled work: $125,158.50.

36
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:06,920
Every answer shows the SQL behind it, so the figure can be checked.

37
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:10,920
It only reads. Changes come back as proposals to approve.

38
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:15,920
New business: every enquiry is logged with its source and claim type.

39
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:18,920
Intake shows each enquiry, newest first.

40
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:25,920
The statute of limitations is worked out the day the enquiry arrives: here, 360 days to run.

41
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:32,920
A workflow runs the conflict check and waits for a person to clear it before anyone gives advice.

42
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:37,420
Every matter is one file, and every part of the firm reads from it.

43
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:40,420
1,300 matters in the demo firm.

44
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:44,420
Search runs across the whole database, not just the page on screen.

45
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:50,420
Court, judge, case number, fee terms, the team, and a Privileged mark on every matter.

46
00:03:50,500 --> 00:03:55,420
Open any record read-only, with its linked records and the papers filed under it.

47
00:03:55,500 --> 00:03:59,920
Open a new matter by describing it in plain English.

48
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:04,920
The form fills itself, and nothing is saved until someone checks it.

49
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:09,920
Documents are filed by matter and found by name, by the text inside or by meaning.

50
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:14,920
Confidentiality: each person sees only the parts of the firm their work needs.

51
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:17,920
Enforced by InventDB, the API and the app.

52
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:24,920
On a phone at the courthouse, the calendar and the matter are a tap away.

53
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:28,920
Light or dark, on any screen.

54
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:33,920
The same practice and the same data, wherever the team works.

55
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:38,920
Under the hood: a React and TypeScript app, a thin Python API, and InventDB SOAR.

56
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:43,420
InventDB is the database and the identity provider. No second datastore.

57
00:04:43,500 --> 00:04:48,420
The API keeps no credentials, so row-level security applies to every request.

58
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:51,920
Covered by 1,300+ backend tests and 600+ end-to-end tests.

59
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:56,420
InventDB Legal: the docket, client trust and billing in one place.

60
00:04:56,500 --> 00:04:59,920
Built on InventDB SOAR. inventdb.com
